From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, comctl32_v6: EXPERIMENT - expose CBS_HASSTRINGS in a combo box's style.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream. Experiment only, not for patches/series: it checks a hypothesis
for Inventor's Content Center filter crash (Inventor-for-Linux #45). The
window trees of the same Inventor state on Windows 10 and under Wine
differ in one systematic way: the Content Center dialog's combo boxes
(not owner-drawn) carry CBS_HASSTRINGS in GWL_STYLE on Windows, not in
Wine, which keeps the implied flag only in its own copy. A MEASURE
program decides the real rule before any real patch.

diff --git a/dlls/comctl32_v6/combo.c b/dlls/comctl32_v6/combo.c
index b497c20..744698d 100644
--- a/dlls/comctl32_v6/combo.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32_v6/combo.c
@@ -140,7 +140,11 @@ static LRESULT COMBO_NCCreate(HWND hwnd, LONG style)
                         GetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & ~WS_EX_CLIENTEDGE );
 
 	if( !(style & (CBS_OWNERDRAWFIXED | CBS_OWNERDRAWVARIABLE)) )
+	{
               lphc->dwStyle |= CBS_HASSTRINGS;
+              /* EXPERIMENT: Windows shows the implied style in GWL_STYLE. */
+              SetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE, GetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) | CBS_HASSTRINGS );
+	}
 	if( !(GetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_NOPARENTNOTIFY) )
 	      lphc->wState |= CBF_NOTIFY;
 
